# Nothing reads a .env in the repository root. The backend reads backend/.env only
# (app/config.py resolves it next to the app, and docker-compose.yml's env_file is
# relative to backend/), and the frontend needs no env file locally.
#
# The template is backend/.env.example:
#   cp backend/.env.example backend/.env
#
# A key placed in a root .env is silently ignored; this happened to OPENFIGI_API_KEY and
# to COIN_STATS_API_KEY. This file deliberately lists no keys, so it cannot drift from
# backend/.env.example or invite that mistake again.
